Project: TrustMerge, a Python Git extension (package trustmerge, commands trustmerge and git-trustmerge).
Stack: Python 3.12, typer, rich, pydantic, httpx, pytest. Call git via subprocess only.
Rules:
- Small changes only: one function or file per task.
- Every function gets a pytest test in tests/.
- Never claim a change is tested without evidence; return UNKNOWN instead.
- All LLM calls go through trustmerge/llm.py, with a fake client for tests (TRUSTMERGE_LLM=fake).
- Provenance is stored in git notes under refs/notes/trustmerge.
- No secrets in the repo. No network calls except to localhost Ollama.
- Run pytest -q before finishing any task.
